.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
.Dd November 13, 2026
.Dt NOQTIS-CHUNK 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm noqtis-chunk
.Nd record the chunk digests of a large file, and check a piece of it
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm noqtis chunk pin
.Op Fl -size Ar bytes
.Ar dir file ...
.Nm noqtis chunk check
.Op Fl -at Ar offset
.Op Fl j | Fl -json
.Ar dir file
.Op Ar piece
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Cm pin
reads each
.Ar file
in
.Ar dir
once and records in the data record
.Pq Cm chunks , Xr noqtis-data 5
the SHA-256 of each run of
.Fl -size
bytes (default 1048576; 1024 to 1073741824), the last run short.
The file is not split.
Seal the folder afterwards: the seal covers the digests through the
record.
.Pp
.Cm check
checks
.Ar file ,
or
.Ar piece ,
a part of it whose first byte is byte
.Fl -at
of the file (a multiple of the chunk size; default 0), against the
recorded digests: each whole chunk it holds, and a short last one when
it ends where the file does.
Only that is read, so a range fetched alone, or the part of a file that
survived, can be checked without the rest.
A short run at the end of a piece that is not the file's end is not
checked, and a row says so.
.Pp
To trust the digests without the file, check the record's seal alone:
.Ql noqtis check --only noqtis.data.json .
.Xr noqtis-data 1
.Cm check
checks each file whole against its chunks.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It 0
Recorded; or every chunk read matches.
.It 1
A chunk differs, the piece runs past the file, or it holds no whole
chunk.
.It 2
A usage or file error, or no chunks recorded for
.Ar file .
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ noqtis chunk pin --size 4194304 results data/big.parquet
$ noqtis seal -k me results
$ curl -r 8388608-16777215 -o part https://example.org/big.parquet
$ noqtis check -p me.pub --only noqtis.data.json results
$ noqtis chunk check --at 8388608 results data/big.parquet part
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr noqtis-check 1 ,
.Xr noqtis-data 1 ,
.Xr nqdchunk 3 ,
.Xr noqtis-data 5
